---
# Beam Boy — clang-format config.
#
# Pins the style already used throughout the codebase (2-space indent, 80
# columns, Google-style brace placement) so "format on save" in any editor
# reformats *to* this, instead of silently drifting toward whatever that
# editor's C/C++ extension defaults to when no .clang-format is present. That
# drift is exactly what was happening before this file existed.
BasedOnStyle: Google
ColumnLimit: 80
